From 894032dfd6d345948bc6e5f1c1cd490c7aa0bfed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:59:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 241/243] ipa: rkisp2: Add the lens distortion correction

The ISPP FEC stage resamples the picture through a mesh of source
positions loaded on its mesh device, which no algorithm generated.

Add a DistortionCorrection algorithm that generates the mesh from the
OCamCalib or OpenCV fisheye model given by the tuning file or the
rkisp2 lens controls, with an output focal length that keeps the image
edge nearest to the optical centre so that no blank area appears, and
enables the FEC stage while a model is set. The level blends linearly
between the uncorrected and the fully corrected source position. The
IPA fills a mesh buffer on request from the pipeline handler, and
reports lens control changes so that the pipeline handler can have a
new mesh computed. The FEC block moves out of the static Ispp
parameters.

For the OCamCalib lens of the vendor IQ files the generated mesh is
within 1.2 pixels of the one of the Rockchip mesh generator.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
